# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 4: Brickwork Clifford circuit {#example-4-brickwork-clifford-circuit}"
msgstr "Contoh 4: Brickwork Clifford circuit {#example-4-brickwork-clifford-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example simulates Clifford circuits. This family of circuits is useful because you can design the simulation to have a known expectation value. Specifically, you can design the circuit and the observable so that the expectation value is always 1, as follows:\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini mensimulasikan circuit Clifford. Keluarga circuit ini berguna karena kamu bisa merancang simulasinya agar punya expectation value yang diketahui. Secara spesifik, kamu bisa merancang circuit dan observable sehingga expectation value-nya selalu 1, sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The starting point (the stabilizer):** Start with the vacuum state $|0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$. Applying the Pauli $Z$ or the identity operator to $|0\\rangle$ leaves it unchanged: $Z|0\\rangle = |0\\rangle$ and $I |0\\rangle = |0\\rangle$. Therefore, any Pauli string $P$ that is a tensor product of only $Z$ and $I$ leaves the all-zero state $|0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$ unchanged: $P |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n} = |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$.\n"
msgstr "**Titik awal (stabilizer):** Mulai dari state vakum $|0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$. Menerapkan Pauli $Z$ atau operator identitas ke $|0\\rangle$ tidak mengubahnya: $Z|0\\rangle = |0\\rangle$ dan $I |0\\rangle = |0\\rangle$. Jadi, string Pauli $P$ mana pun yang merupakan tensor product dari hanya $Z$ dan $I$ tidak mengubah state all-zero $|0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$: $P |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n} = |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The Clifford evolution:** Applying the unitary $U_L$ to the state gives $|\\psi\\rangle = U_L |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$. To find an observable whose expectation value for this new state is 1, apply the same unitary transformation to the operator: $O_L = U_L P U_L^{\\dagger}$. This is the Heisenberg picture of quantum mechanics.\n"
msgstr "**Evolusi Clifford:** Menerapkan unitary $U_L$ ke state menghasilkan $|\\psi\\rangle = U_L |0\\rangle^{{\\otimes}n}$. Untuk menemukan observable yang expectation value-nya untuk state baru ini adalah 1, terapkan transformasi unitary yang sama ke operator: $O_L = U_L P U_L^{\\dagger}$. Ini adalah Heisenberg picture dari mekanika kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Why the observable stays a single Pauli string:** If $U_L$ contained non-Clifford gates (such as T gates or arbitrary rotations), $U_L P U_L^\\dagger$ would expand into a sum of many different Pauli strings. You would have to measure many different observables and add them to get 1. However, because the circuit uses only Clifford gates, the Gottesman-Knill theorem guarantees that $U_L P U_L^\\dagger$ maps to exactly one Pauli string (for example, $X Y -Z X$).\n"
msgstr "**Mengapa observable tetap berupa satu string Pauli:** Jika $U_L$ mengandung Gate non-Clifford (seperti Gate T atau rotasi sembarang), $U_L P U_L^\\dagger$ akan meluas menjadi jumlah dari banyak string Pauli yang berbeda. Kamu harus mengukur banyak observable berbeda dan menjumlahkannya untuk mendapatkan 1. Namun, karena circuit hanya memakai Gate Clifford, teorema Gottesman-Knill menjamin bahwa $U_L P U_L^\\dagger$ dipetakan ke tepat satu string Pauli (misalnya, $X Y -Z X$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The mathematical guarantee:** Because of this construction, computing the expectation value is a simple algebraic substitution:\n"
msgstr "**Jaminan matematis:** Karena konstruksi ini, menghitung expectation value hanyalah substitusi aljabar sederhana:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle O_L \\rangle = \\langle \\psi | O_L | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle O_L \\rangle = \\langle \\psi | O_L | \\psi \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Substitute $|\\psi \\rangle$ and $O_L$:\n"
"$$\n"
"(\\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} U_L^{\\dagger})\n"
"(U_L P U_L^{\\dagger})\n"
"(U_L | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Substitusikan $|\\psi \\rangle$ dan $O_L$:\n"
"$$\n"
"(\\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} U_L^{\\dagger})\n"
"(U_L P U_L^{\\dagger})\n"
"(U_L | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n})\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The adjacent $U_L^\\dagger U_L$ terms cancel (they equal the identity $I$):\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} P | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Suku $U_L^\\dagger U_L$ yang bersebelahan saling meniadakan (hasilnya sama dengan identitas $I$):\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} P | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $P$ is a tensor product of only $Z$ and $I$, $P| 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n} = | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n}$, and therefore:\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n} = 1\n"
"$$\n"
"First, design quantum circuits that contain only Clifford gates: the single-qubit gates $H$, $S$, $X$, $Y$, and $Z$, and the two-qubit gate $CZ$. The `create_brickwork_clifford` function takes the number of qubits (`num_qubits`) and `depth` as arguments, and returns a Clifford quantum circuit with the given number of qubits and depth.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena $P$ adalah tensor product dari hanya $Z$ dan $I$, $P| 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n} = | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n}$, sehingga:\n"
"$$\n"
"= \\langle 0 |^{\\otimes n} | 0 \\rangle ^{\\otimes n} = 1\n"
"$$\n"
"Pertama, rancang quantum circuit yang hanya berisi Gate Clifford: Gate satu-qubit $H$, $S$, $X$, $Y$, dan $Z$, serta Gate dua-qubit $CZ$. Fungsi `create_brickwork_clifford` menerima jumlah qubit (`num_qubits`) dan `depth` sebagai argumen, lalu mengembalikan quantum circuit Clifford dengan jumlah qubit dan depth yang diberikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The circuits in this example have 50 qubits (`num_qubits=50`) and varying depths: 30, 35, 40, 45, 50, 55, 60, 65, and 70. For the observables, start from a Pauli string $P$ with Pauli weight 2, that is, two Pauli $Z$ operators at random positions. Then use the `evolve` method to evolve $P$ into $U_{L_i} P U_{L_i}^{\\dagger}$ for the circuit $U_{L_i}$ of each depth. Save the circuits and the corresponding observables in the lists `circuits_list` and `observables_list`, respectively.\n"
msgstr "Circuit dalam contoh ini punya 50 qubit (`num_qubits=50`) dan depth yang bervariasi: 30, 35, 40, 45, 50, 55, 60, 65, dan 70. Untuk observable, mulai dari string Pauli $P$ dengan bobot Pauli 2, yaitu dua operator Pauli $Z$ di posisi acak. Lalu pakai method `evolve` untuk mengevolusikan $P$ menjadi $U_{L_i} P U_{L_i}^{\\dagger}$ untuk circuit $U_{L_i}$ di setiap depth. Simpan circuit dan observable yang sesuai di daftar `circuits_list` dan `observables_list`, secara berurutan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To get the ideal values, run a stabilizer simulation. Create a stabilizer state from each quantum circuit with the Qiskit `StabilizerState` class, which takes a `QuantumCircuit` as input and outputs the corresponding stabilizer state. Then use the `expectation_value` method to calculate the ideal expectation value, which by design is 1 for each circuit and observable pair.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mendapatkan nilai ideal, jalankan simulasi stabilizer. Buat state stabilizer dari setiap quantum circuit dengan class Qiskit `StabilizerState`, yang menerima `QuantumCircuit` sebagai input dan menghasilkan state stabilizer yang sesuai. Lalu pakai method `expectation_value` untuk menghitung expectation value ideal, yang secara desain bernilai 1 untuk setiap pasangan circuit dan observable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, create a list of PUBs named `clifford_pubs` and pass it to `ltm_function` to compute the expectation values on hardware and mitigate them with AI-QEM.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, buat daftar PUB bernama `clifford_pubs` dan berikan ke `ltm_function` untuk menghitung expectation value di hardware dan memitigasinya dengan AI-QEM.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Extract and visualize the results {#extract-and-visualize-the-results-2}"
msgstr "Ekstrak dan visualisasikan hasilnya {#extract-and-visualize-the-results-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the job finishes, collect the expectation values and standard deviations from each PUB result. For every circuit depth, the results include the noisy (unmitigated) values, `noisy_evs` and `noisy_stds`, and the values after mitigation by AI-QEM, `mitigated_evs` and `mitigated_stds`.\n"
msgstr "Setelah job selesai, kumpulkan expectation value dan standar deviasi dari setiap hasil PUB. Untuk setiap depth circuit, hasilnya mencakup nilai noisy (belum dimitigasi), `noisy_evs` dan `noisy_stds`, serta nilai setelah dimitigasi oleh AI-QEM, `mitigated_evs` dan `mitigated_stds`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then use the `plot_clifford_results` function to plot the expectation value against the circuit depth. The plot contains the following:\n"
msgstr "Lalu pakai fungsi `plot_clifford_results` untuk memplot expectation value terhadap depth circuit. Plot tersebut berisi hal-hal berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Unmitigated:** The raw expectation values returned by the hardware, shown with error bars of size $\\pm\\sigma$.\n"
msgstr "**Belum dimitigasi:** Expectation value mentah yang dikembalikan hardware, ditampilkan dengan error bar berukuran $\\pm\\sigma$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Mitigated (AI-QEM):** The expectation values after error mitigation, also shown with error bars.\n"
msgstr "**Dimitigasi (AI-QEM):** Expectation value setelah error mitigation, juga ditampilkan dengan error bar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ideal (stabilizer simulation):** The noiseless expectation value, $\\langle O \\rangle_{\\text{ideal}} = 1$, for all depths.\n"
msgstr "**Ideal (simulasi stabilizer):** Expectation value tanpa noise, $\\langle O \\rangle_{\\text{ideal}} = 1$, untuk semua depth.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Threshold:** A gray band that covers $-0.1 \\le \\langle O \\rangle \\le 0.1$. Values inside this band have no useful signal to mitigate, so they are left unmitigated.\n"
msgstr "**Threshold:** Pita abu-abu yang mencakup $-0.1 \\le \\langle O \\rangle \\le 0.1$. Nilai di dalam pita ini tidak punya sinyal yang berguna untuk dimitigasi, jadi dibiarkan tanpa mitigasi.\n"

